# kubernetes/apps

Workloads, one directory per module, reconciled by the `apps` Flux Kustomization.

Every module here is **generic platform machinery**, not an application you run
for its own sake. Your actual apps go in one of two places:

- **in this repo** — add a directory following the same shape (namespace,
  workload, NetworkPolicy, VPA, kustomization) and list it in
  `kustomization.yaml`;
- **in their own repo** — onboard it as a tenant, so it deploys from its own git
  history with its own CI. See
  `kubernetes/clusters/{{ cluster_name }}/tenants/README.md`.

